#
# STXLIB-PI4 -- the appliance kernel for the Raspberry Pi 4 Model B (BCM2711,
# arm64), booted by the Pi firmware, U-Boot's UEFI and FreeBSD's loader.efi
# (C1 step S4, Pi image: appliance/disk/build_pi4_image.sh).
#
# Method: as STXLIB-VM, FreeBSD's arm64 GENERIC (releng/15.2 at
# fb9033d2876d) minus what the appliance does not need, each cut with its
# reason. Kept for the Pi 4: SOC_BRCM_BCM2838 (BCM2711) and its drivers,
# compiled by that option in sys/conf/files.arm64:569-594: genet Ethernet
# (if_genet.c, needs mii/miibus), the SD controllers (bcm2835_sdhci.c and
# bcm2835_sdhost.c, device sdhci, with mmc and mmcsd), the PCIe bridge and
# the VL805 USB 3 controller (bcm2838_pci.c, bcm2838_xhci.c, device pci and
# xhci, with usb and the keyboard/HID stack), the firmware mailbox, clocks,
# GPIO, DMA, watchdog, random and cpufreq. SOC_BRCM_BCM2837 stays as well:
# mbox_if.m, which bcm2835_mbox.c needs, is compiled only under that option
# (files.arm64:414). The console is the PL011 on GPIO 14/15 (pl011, from
# std.arm64), chosen by the device tree's stdout-path; uart_mu (the mini
# UART) stays for a firmware configuration that uses it.
#
# Cuts that are not safe on the Pi and so are not taken from STXLIB-VM:
# genet's PHY bus (mdio, mii, miibus), mmc and mmcsd, sdhci, gpioled and
# gpioregulator (the Pi 4's SD I/O voltage regulator is a GPIO regulator in
# its device tree), cpufreq.
#
include 	"GENERIC"
ident		STXLIB-PI4

# --- 1a. SoC support: every std.<soc> entry not on the Pi 4 (the list is
# STXLIB-VM's, without std.broadcom, which follows).

# std.al: not on the Raspberry Pi 4
nodevice	al_ccu	# Alpine Cache Coherency Unit
nodevice	al_nb_service	# Alpine North Bridge Service
nodevice	al_iofic	# I/O Fabric Interrupt Controller
nodevice	al_serdes	# Serializer/Deserializer
nodevice	al_udma	# Universal DMA
nodevice	al_pci	# Annapurna Alpine PCI-E
nodevice	al_eth	# Annapurna Alpine Ethernet NIC

# std.allwinner: not on the Raspberry Pi 4
